    "body": "Unfortunately I think this exposes this step now causing another issue (for the same test) where this step aborts, causing promises to reject with AbortError and navigateerror to fire.\r\n\r\nSequence here being:\r\n\r\n- Step 5 event taskInstalls the event and tracker (awaited)\r\n- Step 8.3 clearing task no longer queued due to it being same-document\r\n- Step 8.4 abort task sees the still live event and aborts it\r\n\r\nSpeaking in terms of my original report, I think we're hitting this case now:\r\n\r\n> 8.4: Ongoing navigation for navigable set to traversal.\r\n> \"Inform the navigation API about aborting navigation\" entered.\r\n> \"TASK B\" queued with the abort loop. **_Does nothing as \"TASK A\" runs first nulling navigate event_**\r\n\r\nAs \"TASK A\" is no longer doing the nulling.\r\n\r\nAnd the cases we need to be careful about in terms of hitting this are:\r\n\r\n- step 8.4: null -> \"traversal\"\r\n- step 14.10.1: \"traversal\" -> null",
