    "body": "This is quite confusing wording wise, but perhaps:\r\n\r\n\"Set the ongoing navigation for navigable to \"traversal\"\" could become \"Set navigable's ongoing navigation to \"traversal\"\" (and null for 14.10.1)\r\n\r\ni.e we don't go through the informing the navigation API parts? It works for this narrow case, but I'm not sure if there are other situations where it matters (if we could get away with that it would be really nice to have less tasks to order)",
